@startuml deployment
title Deployment (docker compose)

skinparam shadowing false

actor "Client / curl /\nscripts" as client

node "Docker host" {
  node "postgres\n<<container>>\npostgis/postgis:16-3.4\n(linux/amd64)" as pg {
    database "canals DB\nschemas: public, payment_mock" as db
  }
  storage "pgdata\n<<volume>>" as vol

  node "migrate\n<<one-shot container>>\ncanals-api image\nnode dist/db/migrate.js" as migrate
  node "seed\n<<one-shot container>>\ncanals-api image\nnode dist/db/seed.js" as seed

  node "api\n<<container>>\ncanals-api image\nnode dist/server.js\n:3000, healthcheck GET /health" as api {
    component "HTTP routes" as routes
    component "sweeper / reconciler /\noutbox poller (setInterval)" as jobs
  }

  node "payment-mock\n<<container>>\ncanals-payment-mock image\n:4000, healthcheck GET /health" as mock
}

client --> api : HTTP :3000
client ..> mock : HTTP :4000 (inspection)
db -- vol
migrate --> db : SQL (advisory lock,\nschema_migrations)
seed --> db : SQL (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING)
api --> db : SQL (pg pool, 10 conns,\nlock 5s / statement 10s /\nidle-in-tx 30s timeouts)
api --> mock : HTTP (3s timeout)
mock --> db : SQL (own schema)

note right of migrate
  Start-up order (depends_on):
  1. postgres: service_healthy (pg_isready)
  2. migrate: completed_successfully
  3. seed: completed_successfully
  4. api
  payment-mock only waits for postgres
  docker compose up --wait returns once
  api and payment-mock are healthy
end note

note as production
  Production mapping (see README):
  API -> ECS/Fargate or Lambda + API Gateway (CDK)
  jobs -> EventBridge Scheduler -> Lambda
  postgres -> RDS / Aurora PostgreSQL + PostGIS behind RDS Proxy
  outbox -> EventBridge bus
end note

@enduml
